        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Check Source",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "return $context.$triggers.REST.$input.prjPjbRoutingContext;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772424930071"
          },
          "code": "PRJ_PJB_CODE_CHECK_SOURCE",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1772424930071",
          "id": "2901800000000",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Relevancy Checker"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772425007889"
          },
          "code": "PRJ_PJB_LLM_RELEVANCY_CHECKER",
          "id": "1779846287008",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1779846287010_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "ROLE\nYou are a relevancy and intent classifier for the \"Project Contract Invoicing Assistant\".\n\nTASK\nClassify the current user input and return only valid JSON containing:\n- prior invoice context\n- effective invoice filters\n- user intent\n- action\n- Relevant\n- RelevantVague\n\nINPUTS\n- Goal: {{$context.$variables.prjPjbVarConvGoal}}\n- CurrentState: {{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvCurrentState}}\n- ChatHistory: {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n- CurrentUserInput: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n- routingContext: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.prjPjbRoutingContext}}\n- currentUserMessage: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.message}}\n- relevantInfo: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.prjPjbRelevantInfo}}\n\nGENERAL RULES\n- Return only valid JSON. No markdown. No explanation.\n- Use null for unknown values.\n- Preserve prior values exactly as provided.\n- Do not invent values.\n- Prefer `relevantInfo.atomicAgentDetails.contextDetails` over chat history for prior invoice context.\n- Use chat history only for follow-up interpretation, not to override explicit prior invoice context.\n- For Act flows, do not inherit `business_unit`, `customer`, `project`, `invoiceStatus`, `invoiceDate`, or `receivablesInvoiceNumber` from chat history unless explicitly present in `relevantInfo.atomicAgentDetails.contextDetails`.\n- When `routingContext = \"RedwoodUI\"`, always populate every `Old*` field from `relevantInfo.atomicAgentDetails.contextDetails` when present.\n- If `relevantInfo.atomicAgentDetails.contextDetails.Intent` is missing, use `relevantInfo.atomicAgentDetails.atomicAgentContext` as fallback for `OldIntent`.\n\nPRIOR INVOICE CONTEXT\nWhen `routingContext = \"RedwoodUI\"`, derive prior invoice context only from `relevantInfo.atomicAgentDetails.contextDetails`.\n\nMap:\n- `OldBusinessUnit = business_unit`\n- `OldCustomer = customer`\n- `OldProject = project`\n- `OldContractNumber = ContractNumber`\n- `OldInvoiceStatus = invoiceStatus`\n- `OldInvoiceDate = invoiceDate`\n- `OldInvoiceNumber = invoiceNumber`\n- `OldReceivablesInvoiceNumber = receivablesInvoiceNumber`\n- `OldBillingPeriodStartDate = billing_period.start_date`\n- `OldBillingPeriodEndDate = billing_period.end_date`\n- `OldBillingPeriodRawText = billing_period.raw_text`\n- `OldIntent = Intent`\n- `OldAction = action`\n- `OldFiltersApplied = relevantInfo.atomicAgentDetails.filters` if present, else null\n\nCURRENT FILTER EXTRACTION\nExtract from `currentUserMessage` when explicitly present: `business_unit`, `customer`, `project`, `ContractNumber`, `invoiceStatus`, `invoiceDate`, `invoiceNumber`, `receivablesInvoiceNumber`, `billing_period.start_date`, `billing_period.end_date`, `billing_period.raw_text`.\n\nFOLLOW-UP RULES\n1. Redwood retrieval continuation: If `routingContext = \"RedwoodUI\"` and prior invoice context contains at least one non-null effective filter, then generic retrieval follow-ups such as show invoices, list invoices, get invoices, display invoices, show approved invoices, or show draft invoices are relevant continuation requests even when the current message does not restate the filters. Preserve all `Old*` fields, carry forward prior filters unless explicitly changed, set `Relevant = \"Yes\"`, `RelevantVague = \"No\"`, `Intent = \"Get\"`, and `action = \"List\"`.\n\n2. Redwood explicit action continuation: If `routingContext = \"RedwoodUI\"` and the current message explicitly asks to approve, submit, reject, revert, release, transfer, or cancel, preserve all `Old*` fields, derive `Intent` from the explicit action, set `action = \"Act\"`, set `ContractNumber = OldContractNumber` when contract is omitted and `OldContractNumber` exists, treat an explicit invoice number plus missing contract as continuation on the prior contract when `OldContractNumber` exists, and set `Relevant = \"Yes\"` and `RelevantVague = \"No\"`. Example: `approve invoice 1` -> `Intent = \"Approve\"`, `action = \"Act\"`, `invoiceNumber = \"1\"`, `ContractNumber = OldContractNumber` when contract is omitted.\n\n3. Redwood confirmation or negation continuation: If `routingContext = \"RedwoodUI\"`, prior invoice context exists, and the current message is a short follow-up such as yes, yeah, yup, do it, continue, go ahead, proceed, no, don't do it, do not do it, stop, or cancel that, treat it as continuation of the immediately preceding assistant prompt, not as a fresh request. Preserve all `Old*` fields, inspect the immediately preceding assistant message in `ChatHistory`, set `Intent` to the action asked by that assistant message when clear, fall back to `OldIntent` only when that message is unclear, set `ContractNumber = OldContractNumber` when contract is missing and available, set `invoiceNumber = OldInvoiceNumber` when invoice number is missing and available, and set `Relevant = \"Yes\"` and `RelevantVague = \"No\"`. For affirmative replies set `action = \"Act\"`. For negative replies do not convert the reply into a new action request, set `action = OldAction`, and set `message = \"User declined follow-up action\"`.\n\nCONFIRMATION INTENT RESOLUTION\nFor short confirmation or negation replies in RedwoodUI, resolve the pending action from the immediately preceding assistant message first. Examples: `Would you like to release it?` + `Yes` -> `Intent = \"Release\"`, `action = \"Act\"`; `Would you like to approve it?` + `Yes` -> `Intent = \"Approve\"`, `action = \"Act\"`; `Would you like to submit it?` + `Yes` -> `Intent = \"Submit\"`, `action = \"Act\"`; `Would you like to reject it?` + `Yes` -> `Intent = \"Reject\"`, `action = \"Act\"`; `Would you like to revert it to draft?` + `Yes` -> `Intent = \"Revert\"`, `action = \"Act\"`; `Would you like to transfer it?` + `Yes` -> `Intent = \"Transfer\"`, `action = \"Act\"`; `Would you like to cancel it?` + `Yes` -> `Intent = \"Cancel\"`, `action = \"Act\"`. If the immediately preceding assistant message does not clearly ask for a follow-up action, only then fall back to `OldIntent`.\n\nINTENT RULES\n- Set `Intent = \"Get\"` when the user explicitly asks to: get, show, list, display, fetch, retrieve, view, review, lookup, look up, pull up, find, search, query, what are the invoices, or which invoices.\n- Set `Intent = \"Details\"` when the user explicitly asks to: get invoice lines, display invoice lines, get invoice distributions, get detailed invoice, or invoice details.\n- Set `Intent = \"Approve\"` when the user explicitly asks to: approve, mark as approved, set status to approved, or complete approval.\n- Set `Intent = \"Submit\"` when the user explicitly asks to: submit, submit for approval, send for approval, route for approval, move to submitted, set status to submitted, or initiate approval.\n- Set `Intent = \"Release\"` when the user explicitly asks to: finalize, confirm, close invoice, complete invoice, sign off invoice, publish invoice, or release invoice.\n- Set `Intent = \"Revert\"` when the user explicitly asks to: return to draft, move to draft, revert, move to edit mode, prepare for corrections, withdraw invoice, stop invoice, or recall invoice.\n- Set `Intent = \"Reject\"` when the user explicitly asks to: reject approval, reject invoice, mark as reject, or set status as reject.\n- Set `Intent = \"Cancel\"` when the user explicitly asks to: void invoice, cancel invoice, invalidate invoice, nullify invoice, or issue a credit memo.\n- Set `Intent = \"Transfer\"` when the user explicitly asks to: send to AR, transfer to AR, interface to AR, push to AR, send to receivables, transfer to receivables, interface to receivables, generate AR transaction, or create AR invoice.\n- If the current message is generic but prior invoice context exists and the message is a follow-up list or show request, set `Intent = \"Get\"`.\n- If the current message is a short confirmation or negation reply in RedwoodUI, do not derive `Intent` from the reply text alone. Resolve it from the immediately preceding assistant message first, and only then fall back to `OldIntent`.\n- If multiple action intents are present, set `Intent = null` and `AmbiguityReasonCode = \"MULTIPLE_ACTIONS\"`.\n\nACTION RULES\n- Set `action = \"List\"` when `Intent` is `Get` or `Details`.\n- Set `action = \"Act\"` when `Intent` is `Approve`, `Submit`, `Reject`, `Revert`, `Release`, `Transfer`, or `Cancel`.\n- Otherwise set `action = null`.\n\nSTATUS RULES\n- Allowed canonical invoice statuses are `DRAFT`, `APPROVAL_REJECTED`, `APPROVED`, `SUBMITTED`, `RELEASED`, `TRANSFERRED`, and `ACCEPTED`.\n- Normalize status variants as follows: draft, in draft, unsubmitted, not submitted, work in progress, wip, preliminary, or saved -> `DRAFT`; approval rejected, rejected in approval, rejected by approver, approver rejected, rejected during approval, failed approval, approval failure, or returned rejected -> `APPROVAL_REJECTED`; approved, approval complete, fully approved, approved by approver, approved in workflow, or passed approval -> `APPROVED`; submitted, submitted for approval, pending approval, awaiting approval, in approval, or under approval review -> `SUBMITTED`; finalize, released, confirmed, completed invoice, or published invoice -> `RELEASED`; transferred, transferred to AR, interfaced to receivables, or interfaced to AR -> `TRANSFERRED`; accepted, tie back, or confirmed invoice acceptance -> `ACCEPTED`.\n- Guardrail: `approved invoices`, `submitted invoices`, and `transferred invoices` used as filters are retrieval filters, not actions.\n- If the user asks for invoices in all statuses, including all statuses, any status, every status, different statuses, distinct statuses, or by status, set `invoiceStatus = null`, do not mark it invalid, and treat it as a valid broad retrieval filter.\n- If an invalid invoice status is mentioned, set `invoiceStatus = null` and `AmbiguityReasonCode = \"INVALID_STATUS\"`.\n\nRELEVANCY PRECEDENCE RULES\nApply in this exact order:\n1. If `routingContext = \"RedwoodUI\"` and prior invoice context contains at least one non-null effective filter, and the current message is a generic follow-up retrieval request, set `Relevant = \"Yes\"` and `RelevantVague = \"No\"`.\n2. If `routingContext = \"RedwoodUI\"` and the current message is a short confirmation, continuation, or negation reply, and prior invoice context exists, set `Relevant = \"Yes\"` and `RelevantVague = \"No\"`, resolve `Intent` from the immediately preceding assistant message first and fall back to `OldIntent` only if unclear, and for affirmative replies set `action = \"Act\"`.\n3. If `routingContext = \"RedwoodUI\"` and `OldContractNumber` is non-null and the current message is an action request with `invoiceNumber` but without a new contract number, set `Relevant = \"Yes\"`, `RelevantVague = \"No\"`, and `ContractNumber = OldContractNumber`.\n4. If the current message explicitly requests viewing, listing, searching, detailing, or summarizing invoices with at least one effective filter from either the current message or prior invoice context, set `Relevant = \"Yes\"`.\n5. If the current message is a generic request such as get invoices, show invoices, list invoices, or display invoices, and there are no effective filters in both `currentUserMessage` and `relevantInfo.atomicAgentDetails.contextDetails`, set `Relevant = \"No\"` and `RelevantVague = \"No\"`.\n6. Greetings such as hi, hello, or hey are `Relevant = \"Yes\"`.\n7. Agent capability or help questions are `Relevant = \"Yes\"`.\n8. Irrelevant actions include unrelated ERP or module questions, weather, personal or non-Oracle questions, root cause analysis not tied to invoice support, or requests outside invoice lifecycle support. These are `Relevant = \"No\"`.\n\nVAGUE RULES\n- Only evaluate vagueness when `Relevant = \"Yes\"`.\n- Set `RelevantVague = \"Yes\"` only for: `UNDETERMINED_INPUT`, `MISSING_FILTER_ATTRIBUTE`, `MISSING_FILTER_VALUE`, `FILTER_ATTRIBUTE_NOT_SUPPORTED`, `FILTER_VALUE_TOO_SMALL`, or `MISSING_ACTION_KEYS`.\n- For `MISSING_ACTION_KEYS`, apply only when required keys such as `ContractNumber` or `invoiceNumber` are missing and no usable prior contract context exists.\n- Do not mark short confirmation or negation replies such as yes, no, do it, don't do it, continue, go ahead, proceed, stop, or cancel that as vague when valid prior Redwood invoice context exists.\n- If none of the above apply, set `RelevantVague = \"No\"` and `AmbiguityReasonCode = null`.\n\nOUTPUT\nReturn only valid JSON with this schema:\n\n{\n  \"OldIntent\": <string or null>,\n  \"OldAction\": <string or null>,\n  \"FiltersApplied\": <object or null>,\n  \"OldFiltersApplied\": <object or null>,\n  \"business_unit\": <string or null>,\n  \"customer\": <string or null>,\n  \"project\": <string or null>,\n  \"ContractNumber\": <string or null>,\n  \"invoiceStatus\": <string or null>,\n  \"invoiceDate\": <string or null>,\n  \"invoiceNumber\": <string or null>,\n  \"receivablesInvoiceNumber\": <string or null>,\n  \"billing_period\": {\n    \"start_date\": <string or null>,\n    \"end_date\": <string or null>,\n    \"raw_text\": <string or null>\n  },\n  \"OldBusinessUnit\": <string or null>,\n  \"OldCustomer\": <string or null>,\n  \"OldProject\": <string or null>,\n  \"OldContractNumber\": <string or null>,\n  \"OldInvoiceStatus\": <string or null>,\n  \"OldInvoiceDate\": <string or null>,\n  \"OldInvoiceNumber\": <string or null>,\n  \"OldReceivablesInvoiceNumber\": <string or null>,\n  \"OldBillingPeriodStartDate\": <string or null>,\n  \"OldBillingPeriodEndDate\": <string or null>,\n  \"OldBillingPeriodRawText\": <string or null>,\n  \"Intent\": <string or null>,\n  \"action\": <string or null>,\n  \"AmbiguityReasonCode\": <string or null>,\n  \"RelevantVague\": <string>,\n  \"Relevant\": <string>\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"billing_period\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"additionalProperties\": false,\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"start_date\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"date\" },\n      \"end_date\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"date\" },\n      \"raw_text\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n    },\n    \"required\": []\n  },\n  \"business_unit\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n  \"customer\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n  \"project\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n  \"ContractNumber\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n  \"Intent\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n  \"action\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n  \"message\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n  \"invoiceStatus\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n  \"invoiceDate\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"date\" },\n  \"invoiceNumber\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n  \"receivablesInvoiceNumber\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n  \"ambiguities\": {\n    \"type\": \"array\",\n    \"items\": { \"type\": \"object\" },\n    \"default\": []\n  },\n  \"clarifying_questions\": {\n    \"type\": \"array\",\n    \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n    \"default\": []\n  },\n  \"missingInformation\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n  \"ChatHistory\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n  \"language\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n\n  \"OldBusinessUnit\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n  \"OldCustomer\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n  \"OldProject\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n  \"OldContractNumber\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n  \"OldInvoiceStatus\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n  \"OldInvoiceDate\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"date\" },\n  \"OldInvoiceNumber\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n  \"OldReceivablesInvoiceNumber\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n  \"OldBillingPeriod\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"additionalProperties\": false,\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"start_date\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"date\" },\n      \"end_date\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"date\" },\n      \"raw_text\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n    },\n    \"required\": []\n  },\n\n  \"OldIntent\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n  \"OldAction\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n\n  \"FiltersApplied\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"additionalProperties\": true\n  },\n  \"OldFiltersApplied\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"additionalProperties\": true\n  },\n\n  \"AmbiguityReasonCode\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n  \"RelevantVague\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n  \"Relevant\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
